--- diagnostics ---
SC0433 @83..103 `swap` takes two exclusive spans of `F64`
  note @58..78 the other one
  note `noalias` is a promise about the callee as well as the caller: if the C function aliases the two internally the optimiser may reorder, cache and duplicate accesses across the call, and the answer changes
  note where the library's published contract guarantees they do not overlap — BLAS says so — this is correct as written; where it is silent, declare them `ffi.Pointer[T]`, which carries no attribute
